Let CosmicTextSystem take a caller-built FontSystem.

What: add `CosmicTextSystem::new_with_font_system(FontSystem, &str)` in gpui_wgpu; `new` and
`new_without_system_fonts` become one-line calls to it. No behaviour change for existing callers.

Why: fontdb has no system font discovery on Android, so `new` finds no fonts, and `new_without_system_fonts`
fixes the locale to en-US and cosmic-text's empty Android fallback table. Parallax's Android backend
(parallax-android) reads /system/etc/fonts.xml itself and wants to hand over a `FontSystem` built with
`FontSystem::new_with_locale_and_db_and_fallback`: fonts loaded by path (fontdb memory-maps them), the app's
locale, and a per-script fallback table (CJK by locale, emoji). Today the only other way in is `add_fonts`
with bytes, which keeps cosmic-text's empty fallback table and en-US locale. Until this lands, the published
parallax-android works around it on stock gpui_wgpu (docs/patches.md, "Published crates").

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

